{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453575-al-andalus-cordoba-islamic-spain-~1000-ad","id":1453575,"title":"Al Andalus / Cordoba / \"Islamic Spain\", ~1000 AD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-26T11:34:16-07:00","id":1453575,"title":"Al Andalus / Cordoba / \"Islamic Spain\", ~1000 AD","content":"I'm running an M20 game set in the Caliphate of Cordoba in the year 1000!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Al-Andalus, ruled from the capital in Corboda - the most populous city in the whole world. This is the seat of the Caliph Hisham ll, the leader of an exiled offshoot of the Umayyad Caliphate who once ruled most of the Islamic world.<br /> <br /> PITY THE LORDLESS MAN<br /> <br /> In 2021 we tend to see ourselves as our own property; we may have loyalties to our faith or country, but with post-enlightenment ideals we often conceive of our own personhood as independent.<br /> <br /> This is not the case in the year 1000. People belong to masters, and to their god, and their personhood is pulled in many different directions. A truly independent person who owes no loyalty to anyone is a person who is difficult to trust - who is to stand surety for them?<br /> <br /> COSMOPOLITAN LIFE<br /> <br /> Islamic Arabs stand atop the pile, nearly shoulder to shoulder with other Muslims. Below them are those who are &quot;protected&quot; by their gracious hosts, among them Christians and Jews. &quot;Dhimmi&quot; (non-Muslim citizens) tend to be &quot;people of the book&quot;, and besides paying slightly more tax (known as the Jizya) they essentially have all the rights and protections of a Muslim.<br /> <br /> It is easy to think of the past as a constant slide towards progress, but this is a high point for integration and tolerance in this part of the world. People of various faiths and ethnicities share coin and ideas and break bread with one another. Jews and Christians rank among the bureaucracy and mercantile class. And homosexuality, often seen as the preserve of modern times (and perhaps Classical Italy and Greece) flourishes in this land, with Christians defecting southward to experience freedom (and Bagnos...).<br /> <br /> A GOLDEN AGE OF MAGICK<br /> <br /> Astrology, medicine, alchemy, Islamic mysticism, Kabballah, theology, Hermeticism, mathematics, natural science; this is a time period of great discovery and academic pursuit. Knowledge is not shared equally, but the educated here are amongst the most enlightened in the world.<br /> <br /> <b>ON THIS STAGE WE LAY OUR SCENE...</b> </div> </div> </div>What surprised me is that this part of the world, at this exact time, gets a mention in the M20 corebook. After reading that, and doing some research, I feel decently well equipped to run the game. With that said...<br /> <br /> Advice on running a Mage game set in this time period would be appreciated. I am using M20 rules, with a little bit of DAV20 mixed in for armour and weaponry. Not personally interested in messing around with Pillars; to me the Sphere system perfectly captures &quot;flexible&quot; magick. Do people have any experience running a Mage game in this sort of setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:59:12-07:00","id":1453599,"title":"","content":"You can probably get at least some mileage out of Vampire: The Dark Ages's Iberia by Night. It's about two hundred years after what you're looking for, but is a starting place. There's also the very old Tribunals of Hermes: Iberia from Ars Magica, which isn't the same as Mage (and again, is about two centuries after your time period), but does have some potential Order of Hermes ideas. (The Ars Magica sourcebook Kabbalah: Mythic Judaism, which gives a really good overview of medieval Jews, may also be useful.) All of them are available on drivethru.rpg, though some of the Ars Magica stuff is probably summarized on that game's various fan sites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T18:14:47-07:00","id":1453615,"title":"","content":"It's probably also a good idea to check out <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/shelf/show/al-andalus\" target=\"_blank\">historical books on the subject</a>. Since RPG books tend to focus on what's relevant to their purposes, rather than being a comprehensive examination of the time and place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T08:04:35-07:00","id":1453650,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> I've already done reading around the &quot;real&quot; context as it were, my main interest is in how to integrate the &quot;fictional&quot; history of Mage, and fun things to do with a reality zone like Cordoba <br /> ~1000 AD.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> good idea, I'll take a look!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T15:28:38-07:00","id":1453671,"title":"","content":"The main thing I remember is that <i>House Flambeau</i> has always had a heavy presence in Iberia. While that House has always had a strong strain of Zoroastrian thought running through it (which would technically make them heretics to both Catholics and Muslims), those ideas aren't entirely incompatible with tenets of those faiths. <br /> <i>Houses Bonisagus</i> and <i>Guernicus</i> most likely have members who are interested in certain aspects of Iberia's scholarship and legal codes. Likewise, more than a few members of <i>House Jerbiton</i> are attracted to the region's culture and artwork. <br /> <br /> As far as the Old Faith/Verbena, There's a number of strata to mine for ideas. There's the Basque cultures around the Pyrenees. Western Iberia was home to a group of Indo-Europeans called the Lusitanians. They were conquered during the Roman Republic period and several of their gods incorporated into the greater Roman pantheon. And after said Romans came the Visigoth kingdoms, with their own religion. <br /> <br /> With the Messianic Voices/Celestial Chorus, besides the Catholic and Muslim faiths, there are probably a few remnants of Visigoth Arianism Christianity. Also some aspects of the Lusitanian sun goddess got incorporated into some of the local aspects of veneration of the Virgin Mary. The Cabal of Pure Thought are probably pretty staunchly Catholic, although just in my own head cannon, I have a branch of them who broke off and became a Muslim version of the Cabal. <br /> <br /> Iberia's extensive trade routes, markets, and commercial laws are likely to attract members of what used to be the Cults of Mercury and later became the High Guild. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T17:16:58-07:00","id":1453674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453575-al-andalus-cordoba-islamic-spain-~1000-ad?p=1453671#post1453671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing I remember is that <i>House Flambeau</i> has always had a heavy presence in Iberia. While that House has always had a strong strain of Zoroastrian thought running through it (which would technically make them heretics to both Catholics and Muslims), those ideas aren't entirely incompatible with tenets of those faiths.<br /> <i>Houses Bonisagus</i> and <i>Guernicus</i> most likely have members who are interested in certain aspects of Iberia's scholarship and legal codes. Likewise, more than a few members of <i>House Jerbiton</i> are attracted to the region's culture and artwork.<br /> <br /> As far as the Old Faith/Verbena, There's a number of strata to mine for ideas. There's the Basque cultures around the Pyrenees. Western Iberia was home to a group of Indo-Europeans called the Lusitanians. They were conquered during the Roman Republic period and several of their gods incorporated into the greater Roman pantheon. And after said Romans came the Visigoth kingdoms, with their own religion.<br /> <br /> With the Messianic Voices/Celestial Chorus, besides the Catholic and Muslim faiths, there are probably a few remnants of Visigoth Arianism Christianity. Also some aspects of the Lusitanian sun goddess got incorporated into some of the local aspects of veneration of the Virgin Mary. The Cabal of Pure Thought are probably pretty staunchly Catholic, although just in my own head cannon, I have a branch of them who broke off and became a Muslim version of the Cabal.<br /> <br /> Iberia's extensive trade routes, markets, and commercial laws are likely to attract members of what used to be the Cults of Mercury and later became the High Guild.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's really helpful, thanks!<br /> <br /> Indigenous basque peoples with old faith &quot;witches&quot; and &quot;druids&quot; could be very interesting, especially when in conflict or collaboration with the magi of more mainstream and acceptable Cordoban practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T03:18:50-07:00","id":1453688,"title":"","content":"This year there'll be an actualization of Tribunals of Hermes: Iberia (in spanish). <br /> <br /> The principal Alliance of House of Flambeau was in Val Negra, in the south of Pyrenees till XIIIth century. The Alliance of Duresca is dominated by House Guernicus/Quaesitor. There's a faction of invocateurs of djinns in House ex-Miscelanea from Al-Andalus. House of Diedne had presence in the old kingdom of Galicia, in the northwest of the iberic peninsule.<br /> <br /> In Dark Ages: Grimoire there's a mention of the Ahl-i-Batin in Cordoba.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T19:42:39-07:00","id":1453738,"title":"","content":"I presume that the Islamic areas of the region will include all the various groups within the Web of Faith to one degree or another. The House of the Crescent Moon, the Batini, the collectors of light, Ecstatic dervishes, shaman/spirit-talkers, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T03:25:11-07:00","id":1453747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453575-al-andalus-cordoba-islamic-spain-~1000-ad?p=1453738#post1453738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that the Islamic areas of the region will include all the various groups within the Web of Faith to one degree or another. The House of the Crescent Moon, the Batini, the collectors of light, Ecstatic dervishes, shaman/spirit-talkers, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Picatrix is going to be written, or collected into a single book from many sources, in this time period. As a result lots of different types of Mages will be collaborating and sharing ideas in this time and place, and fighting when the ideas shared are anathema. So yes lots of different types of Magi about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}